# Package examples

Runnable examples live in `packages/<pkg>/examples/`. They are the **source of truth** for short README snippets; longer or niche demos stay in `examples/` only.

## Which packages

Most active library packages have an `examples/` folder and `examples` / `examples:build` scripts in `package.json`. Not every workspace package does (e.g. `binarytree`, `testdata`, fixture submodules). When adding a new library package, follow the existing pattern.

## Layout

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `examples/*.ts` | Runnable Node examples (CI) |
| `examples/browser.html` | Semi-automated browser run (see file for dev-server steps) |
| `examples/helpers/`, `examples/data/` | Shared helpers/fixtures — **not** executed by the runner |
| `examples/<subdir>/` | Optional grouping (EVM `precompiles/`, `opcodes/`; MPT `merkle_patricia_trees/`) |

**Nested example folders:** `scripts/examples-runner.ts` only reads **one directory level** (`.ts` / `.cts` files). Nested example dirs need an extra runner invocation in the package `examples` script — see `@ethereumjs/evm`:

```json
"examples": "tsx ../../scripts/examples-runner.ts -- evm && tsx ../../scripts/examples-runner.ts -- evm precompiles && tsx ../../scripts/examples-runner.ts -- evm opcodes"
```

Prefer flat `examples/` when possible; use nested folders only when the set is large or clearly grouped.

## README embedding (embedme)

Short examples that fit a docs section are embedded in the package `README.md` via [embedme](https://github.com/zackarychapple/embedme).

1. Edit the file under `examples/` (never hand-edit embedded code blocks in the README).
2. In the README, keep a fence whose first line is the embedme marker, e.g. `// ./examples/simple.ts`.
3. Sync: `npm run examples:build` in the package (`npx embedme README.md`).

Embedme adds the header comment automatically. Pick README candidates that are short and map cleanly to a topic; link to `examples/` for the rest.

## Writing runnable examples

CI runs `npm run examples --if-present --workspaces` (`.github/workflows/examples.yml`, gated from `build.yml`). The runner **dynamic-imports** each `.ts`/`.cts` file in the target folder — there is no `main()` discovery.

- Execute on import: top-level code, or `void main()` / `main().catch(...)` at the bottom.
- Do not rely on manual `tsx examples/foo.ts` only; it must pass the automated runner.
- Avoid interactive prompts, open-ended network calls, or env secrets required in CI.
- Helpers (`helpers/`, `data/`, `.js`/`.cjs`/`.mts` demos) are imported by examples; only `.ts`/`.cts` at the runner target path are executed directly.

Local check: `npm run examples` in the touched package.

## Browser examples

`examples/browser.html` loads a representative `.ts` module in the browser. Convention for active browser-facing packages; some older packages may lack it. Typical flow: build the package, start the local dev server from the package root (see `browser.html`), open `/examples/browser.html`, inspect the dev console.

## Agent checklist

When changing examples:

1. Edit `examples/` source files.
2. If the example is README-embedded, run `npm run examples:build` in that package and commit the README diff.
3. Run `npm run examples` locally.
4. If adding a new nested folder of runnable `.ts` files, extend the package `examples` script (and document the folder in the README if user-facing).
5. Run `npm run tsc` and spellcheck on touched files (`typecheck.mdc`, `spellcheck.mdc`).
